{
  "format": "srwb",
  "version": "1.0",
  "notebook": {
    "name": "Prolog Generates Lua: Compiler Demo",
    "cells": [
      {
        "type": "markdown",
        "code": "# Prolog Generates Lua\n\nThis workbook demonstrates UnifyWeaver compiling Prolog predicates into **Lua** code.\n\nThe workflow:\n1. Define Prolog predicates (facts + rules)\n2. UnifyWeaver detects the recursion pattern (transitive closure)\n3. The compiler generates idiomatic Lua with tables and BFS traversal\n4. Execute the generated Lua code in the Lua kernel\n\n**Requires:** Install the UnifyWeaver package first (Browse Packages).\n\n**Note:** The generated Lua reads from stdin by default. We strip the CLI section and seed the facts directly for in-notebook use.",
        "language": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "% Load UnifyWeaver compiler modules\n['../init'].\n:- use_module(unifyweaver(core/recursive_compiler)).",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "load_compiler"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "% Define a family tree as Prolog facts\n:- dynamic parent/2, ancestor/2.\n\nparent(alice, bob).\nparent(bob, charlie).\nparent(bob, diana).\nparent(charlie, eve).\nparent(diana, frank).\n\n% Transitive closure: ancestor(X, Y) if X is an ancestor of Y\nancestor(X, Y) :- parent(X, Y).\nancestor(X, Y) :- parent(X, Z), ancestor(Z, Y).",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "family_tree"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "% Compile ancestor/2 to Lua\ncompile_recursive(ancestor/2, [target(lua)], FullCode),\n% Strip the CLI section (stdin reading) — we'll seed facts manually\n(   sub_string(FullCode, Before, _, _, \"-- Read parent facts\") \n->  sub_string(FullCode, 0, Before, _, CoreCode)\n;   CoreCode = FullCode\n),\n% Build the final code: core functions + seeded facts + queries\natomic_list_concat([\n    CoreCode,\n    '\\n-- Seed facts from Prolog\\n',\n    'add_fact(\"alice\", \"bob\")\\n',\n    'add_fact(\"bob\", \"charlie\")\\n',\n    'add_fact(\"bob\", \"diana\")\\n',\n    'add_fact(\"charlie\", \"eve\")\\n',\n    'add_fact(\"diana\", \"frank\")\\n',\n    '\\n-- Query: all descendants of alice\\n',\n    'local results = find_all(\"alice\")\\n',\n    'print(\"Descendants of alice: \" .. table.concat(results, \", \"))\\n',\n    '\\n-- Query: is alice ancestor of eve?\\n',\n    'print(\"alice -> eve: \" .. tostring(check(\"alice\", \"eve\")))\\n',\n    'print(\"alice -> frank: \" .. tostring(check(\"alice\", \"frank\")))\\n'\n], LuaCode),\nnb_write('lua_output', '.code', LuaCode).",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "compile_to_lua"
      },
      {
        "type": "markdown",
        "code": "## Generated Lua Code\n\nThe cell below contains the Lua code generated by UnifyWeaver.\nIt includes:\n- Table-based adjacency list (`rel`)\n- BFS graph traversal (`find_all`)\n- Reachability check (`check`)\n- Seeded family tree facts\n\nRun it to compute ancestors!",
        "language": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "-- This cell will be populated by the compiler.\n-- Run the 'compile_to_lua' cell above first.",
        "language": "lua",
        "name": "lua_output"
      }
    ]
  }
}
